   "skos:definition": "A Jewish movement of the Second Temple period known for careful interpretation and practice of the Torah, the \"tradition of the elders\" and belief in the resurrection; Jesus's frequent conversation partners and critics in the Gospels, Paul's own party, and forerunners of the later rabbis.",
